hern Europe. Its establishment coincided with the rise of political parties that aimed to represent the growing middle class and to challenge the dominance of the traditional elite in Swedish politics. Key figures in its formation included Hjalmar Branting and other early 20th-century political leaders who sought to merge liberal economic policies with social responsibility, marking a shift toward a more inclusive political framework in Sweden.

